{
  "statement": "A message typed while a question is open is an answer only when it plainly gives the field, read against today: a vague when is not a date, a value has to be one the question can take, and a message that also says something else is an answer that is not the whole message, so the rest still files.",
  "why": "The answer runs the smallest call there is, before the classifier, on the message and the question alone. It fails safe: a value that does not hold up closes the question and the words file, so nothing is lost either way.",
